        <h2>A little about me</h2>
        <p>I’ve explored mathematical models for discrete problems through computational experiments, including image-based graph extraction and QUBO formulations for graph partitioning. I also enjoy teaching, community activities, and trying unfamiliar tools and ideas.</p>
        <p>My personal motto is simple: <strong>“Trying new things, learning as I go.”</strong> I enjoy stepping into unfamiliar areas, asking questions, and improving through practice. I don’t expect every experiment to work the first time; I value what the process teaches me.</p>
      </section>
